resume_path: RESUME.md
api_keys:
  anthropic: ''
  rapidapi: ''
model: claude-sonnet-4-6
match_threshold: 55
profile: |
  Your professional summary here. Include:
  - Years of experience and key domains
  - Current role and company
  - Core technical skills
  - Leadership experience
  - Notable achievements
  - Education background
target_roles: |
  Describe the types of roles you're targeting. Include ideal titles,
  company types, industries, and what matters most to you in a role.
search_queries:
  - VP of Engineering
  - Head of Product
  - Director of AI
  - Chief Technology Officer
role_keywords:
  - vp
  - vice president
  - head of
  - director
  - principal
  - chief
  - cto
  - staff
startup_role_keywords:
  - founder
  - founding
  - cofounder
career_pages:
  - company: Anthropic
    url: https://www.anthropic.com/careers
    category: ai
greenhouse_boards:
  - company: Cloudflare
    board_token: cloudflare
    category: dev_tools
lever_boards:
  - company: Spotify
    board_token: spotify
    category: big_tech
prompts:
  matching_system: 'You are a job-matching assistant. You evaluate job listings for
    fit with a specific candidate.

    Return ONLY valid JSON — no markdown fences, no commentary.

    '
  matching: 'Evaluate each job for fit with this candidate.


    ## Candidate Profile

    {profile}


    ## Target Roles

    {target_roles}


    ## Scoring (0-100)

    - Role level alignment (40 pts): VP / Director / Head / Principal / C-level?

    - Skills match (30 pts): AI/ML, architecture, platform, leadership, design systems?

    - Industry relevance (20 pts): Health tech, AI, or top-tier tech company?

    - Remote fit (10 pts): Truly remote-friendly for US-based candidate?


    ## Jobs

    {jobs_json}


    Return a JSON array of objects with keys: id (int), score (int 0-100), reason
    (string, 1-2 sentences), gaps (string, 1 sentence about skill/experience gaps
    or "" if none).

    Include ALL jobs with their scores, even low-scoring ones.

    '
  resume_tailoring: 'Customize this resume for the role below.


    Rules:

    1. Keep all facts truthful — never fabricate experience, titles, or dates

    2. Rewrite the Summary (2-3 sentences) to speak directly to this role

    3. Reorder and adjust emphasis of bullet points to foreground relevant experience

    4. You may trim less-relevant bullets to keep the resume focused

    5. Preserve the markdown format exactly

    6. Aim for 2-page length when rendered


    ## Role

    Title: {title}

    Company: {company}

    Description:

    {description}


    ## Original Resume

    {resume}


    Return ONLY the customized resume markdown. No commentary, no fences.

    '
  cover_letter: 'Write a cover letter for this application.


    Rules:

    1. 3-4 paragraphs, conversational but professional

    2. Open with genuine interest in the company or role — not generic flattery

    3. Connect 2-3 specific experiences from the candidate''s background to the role''s
    needs

    4. Close with forward-looking enthusiasm

    5. Don''t rehash the resume — add perspective on why this role, this company,
    right now

    6. Use a modern opening ("Hi [Company] team," or similar) — not "Dear Hiring Manager"

    7. Under 300 words


    ## Role

    Title: {title}

    Company: {company}

    Description:

    {description}


    ## Candidate Background (summary)

    {profile}


    Return ONLY the cover letter text. No commentary, no fences.

    '
  humanize: "Rewrite the following text so it reads like a human wrote it, not an\
    \ AI.\n\nRules:\n1. Preserve ALL factual content, names, dates, titles, and structure\
    \ exactly\n2. Break up formulaic sentence patterns — vary sentence length and\
    \ rhythm\n3. Replace generic AI filler (\"leverage\", \"spearheaded\", \"passionate\
    \ about\",\n   \"proven track record\", \"uniquely positioned\", \"I'm excited\
    \ to\", \"drives me\")\n   with specific, plain language\n4. Avoid em dashes (—\
    ) unless they genuinely fit the sentence better than\n   a comma, period, or parenthetical.\
    \ Most of the time, they don't.\n5. Cut unnecessary intensifiers (\"genuinely\"\
    , \"deeply\", \"truly\", \"incredibly\")\n6. Don't start multiple paragraphs with\
    \ \"I\" or \"At [Company]\"\n7. Keep the same tone and register — don't make it\
    \ more casual or more formal\n8. For resumes: preserve the exact markdown format\n\
    9. For cover letters: keep it under the same word count\n\n## Text to rewrite\n\
    {text}\n\nReturn ONLY the rewritten text. No commentary, no fences.\n"
sources:
  remotive: true
  jsearch: true
  greenhouse: true
  lever: true
  career_pages: true
  hn_who_is_hiring: true
  yc_jobs: true
location: remote
pdf_css: ''
